🔹 Numeric Streams & Reductions:-

Task 1 : ==> Calculate the sum of a list of integers using reduce.

   List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(10, 5, 3, 7, 2, 10, 5, 8, 9, 0, -3, 4);
   System.out.println(numbers.stream().reduce(0, (x, y) -> x + y));


Task 2 : ==> Find the maximum and minimum value in a list.

   List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(10, 5, 3, 7, 2, 10, 5, 8, 9, 0, -3, 4);
   System.out.println("max is: " +numbers.stream().max(Integer::max).get() + ", min is: " +numbers.stream().min(Integer::min).get());


Task 3 : ==> Calculate the average of a list of doubles.

   List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(10, 5, 3, 7, 2, 10, 5, 8, 9, 0, -3, 4);
   System.out.println(numbers.stream().mapToInt(x -> x).average().getAsDouble() );

Task 4 : ==> Multiply all integers in a list together using reduce.

   List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(10, 5, 3, 7, 2, 10, 5, 8, 9, 0, -3, 4);
   System.out.println(numbers.stream().reduce(1, (x, y) -> x * y) );

Task 5 : ==> Count how many numbers are positive in a list.

